fragment:

  - The parameters should be generated by LLM according to the context.
  - "action_id" is not sequential identifier, it must match the number in parentheses of the chosen action.
Exemples:
SET_TEXT (3) == "action_id": "3"
CLICK (4) == "action_id": "4"
LONG_CLICK (2) == "action_id": "2"
BACK (5) == "action_id": "5"

Your response MUST follow this schema - a JSON object with the following structure:
{
  "actions": [
    {
      "action_id": "5",
      "action_text": "CLICK (5)",
      "params": {},
      "explanation": "Opening dropdown to reveal options"
    },
    {
      "action_id": "2",
      "action_text": "SET_TEXT (2)",
      "params": {"text": "test@example.com"},
      "explanation": "Filling email field with valid format"
    }
    // Additional related actions...
  ]
}

SPINNER EXAMPLE - Only open dropdown in current batch:
{
  "actions": [
    {
      "action_id": "3",
      "action_text": "CLICK (3)",
      "params": {},
      "explanation": "Opening language spinner - options will be available in next interaction"
    }
  ]
}

DO NOT include any additional text outside of the JSON object. Your response must be valid JSON that can be parsed directly.
